# Audit events (Permanent)

## Law

Security- and workflow-sensitive actions append an **`audit_events`** row (PostgreSQL). Never soft-delete audit rows. Never log secrets (OTP, tokens, raw license keys, payment card data).

## Locked actions (codes)

| Action | When | `businessId` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `auth.login` | OTP verify success | `null` |
| `business.create` | Business created | set |
| `business.delete` | Business soft-deleted | set |
| `billing.payment.succeeded` | Payment verified → paid | set |
| `billing.license.activated` | SELF_HOSTED install license activated | `null` |
| `export.pdf.enqueued` | PDF export job queued | set |
| `document.delete` | Document soft-deleted | set |
| `document.workflow.submit` | draft → review | set |
| `document.workflow.approve` | review → approved | set |
| `document.workflow.reject` | review → draft | set |
| `document.workflow.publish` | approved → published | set |
| `document.workflow.unpublish` | published → draft | set |
| `document.workflow.reopen` | approved → draft | set |
| `workspace.backup.completed` | Backup ZIP built | set |
| `workspace.restore.completed` | Restore applied | set |
| `membership.invite` | Invitation created | set |
| `membership.accept` | Invitation accepted → membership | set |
| `membership.role_change` | Member role patched | set |
| `membership.remove` | Member removed | set |
| `platform.business.suspend` | SAAS platform admin suspends Business | set |
| `platform.business.unsuspend` | SAAS platform admin unsuspends Business | set |
| `billing.subscription.grace` | Dunning tick persists grace | set |
| `billing.subscription.expired` | Dunning tick persists expired | set |
| `billing.dunning.notice` | Dunning SMS notice recorded | set |

Canonical codes: `AuditActions` in `@vdb/shared-types`.

## Shape

- Columns: `business_id?`, `user_id?`, `action`, `entity_type`, `entity_id?`, `meta` JSONB, `created_at`
- Always set `businessId` for tenant-scoped entities
- `meta` holds non-sensitive context (`from`, `to`, `note`, `amount`, `documentId`, …)
- Writers must not fail the primary write path (`AuditService.log` swallows errors)

## List API (Owner UI)

- `GET /api/businesses/:businessId/audit-events` — JWT + **OWNER/ADMIN** only
- Always constrain to the path business: rows with `businessId = :businessId`, plus **safe** install/user-scoped rows:
  - `auth.login` where `businessId IS NULL` and `userId` is a **member** of that business
  - `billing.license.activated` where `businessId IS NULL` (install-wide; no other-business entities)
- Never return another business’s `businessId` rows
- Filters: `action`, `entityType`, `from` / `to` (ISO date), pagination
